---
import Article from "@/layouts/article.astro"
import { GITHUB_URL, PRIVACY_EMAIL } from "@/lib/links"

const USER_DATA_POLICY_URL =
  "https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
---

<Article title="Privacy">
  <p>
    Wonnet keeps a copy of your mail on your devices and syncs it through a
    server. The apps start on our server; this page says what it stores and why.
    If you run your own server, we see nothing at all.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your mail accounts:</strong> their addresses and providers, and
      what the server needs to reach them: a Gmail refresh token, or a JMAP
      server's address, username and password. Credentials are sealed with
      AES-GCM before they are stored.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your mail:</strong> for each message its sender, recipients,
      subject, date, labels and the names and sizes of its attachments, and the
      bodies of the messages the server has fetched. This is what lets the apps
      sync, search and snooze, and send mail later.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Mail waiting to be sent:</strong> a message you sent with undo
      send or send later stays on the server until it goes out, and for seven
      days after.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your sessions:</strong> each signed-in device has a token. We
      store only its hash. Sign-in codes and links to add another account are
      stored as hashes and expire within minutes.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don't</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your attachments' contents.</strong> We keep their names and sizes
      only. Small images shown inside a message are kept as part of its body.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you read and when.</strong> The site and the apps have no
      analytics and set no tracking cookies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Remote images.</strong> Images in a message stay blocked until you
      ask for them, so senders can't tell that you opened it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    Only to show you your mail and to carry out what you do in the apps:
    archiving, labelling, sending, snoozing. We don't sell it, share it, use it
    for advertising or to train models, and no person reads it unless you ask us
    to for support.
  </p>

  <h2>Google user data</h2>
  <p>
    A Gmail account gives Wonnet access to your email address and to read,
    change and send your mail. Wonnet's use and transfer of information received
    from Google APIs adheres to the{" "}
    <a href={USER_DATA_POLICY_URL}>Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting it</h2>
  <p>
    Removing an account in the apps forgets its credentials and the bodies of
    its mail at once, and stops syncing it. To have everything of yours deleted,
    write to <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>. You can
    check all of this in the <a href={GITHUB_URL}>source</a>.
  </p>
</Article>
